    "image_with_text_FcRb8C": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_tVUetQ": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<strong>Decreasing Libido: The Overlooked Menopause Symptom Women Need to Know</strong>",
            "title_highlight_color": "#53af01",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_dQP6WY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><strong>Women over 40 are TWICE as likely to suffer from sex life compared to men. </strong></p><p>Despite this alarming statistic, many women and doctors often misattribute the symptoms of vagina dryness or low libido to aging or fibromyalgia. </p><p>However, emerging research reveals a different perspective: <strong>the decline in estrogen levels during perimenopause and menopause is a primary cause of low libido. </strong></p><p>This new understanding highlights the need to shift how low libido in middle-aged women is diagnosed and treated, ensuring that hormonal changes are not overlooked.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
