      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_aicbdh": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "<strong>Life After 40: The Impact of Decreasing Estrogen Levels on Women's Health</strong>",
            "title_highlight_color": "#53af01",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_YQWQAJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>As estrogen levels decline, <strong>libido reduces, and oxidative stress increases. </strong></p><p>This hormonal shift also leads to <strong>unexpected weight gain, particularly around the abdomen,</strong> making women unconfident in front of their partners. </p><p>Understanding these changes is crucial for managing the multifaceted effects of lower estrogen on women's health. </p><p>As estrogen levels drop, the resulting changes take a toll on<strong> joint tissues, mood swing and loss of libido. </strong></p><p>This \"Triple Threat\" from hormonal decline causes<strong> significant discomfort and restricts movement</strong>, underscoring the need for awareness and intervention.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
